// =============================================================================
// 00-discover-dependency-types.kql
// RUN THIS FIRST. Nothing else in this library is safe until it returns rows.
// =============================================================================
//
// PURPOSE
//   Enumerate the actual (type, name, target) triples that Copilot Studio emits
//   into Application Insights, so every downstream query can be pinned to the
//   shape this environment really produces instead of an assumed schema.
//
// WHY THIS QUERY EXISTS (open item U8)
//   The sampled 403 record from this customer looks like:
//       type       = "Connector"
//       name       = "Azure AI Search"
//       target     = "shared_azureaisearch/SemanticHybridSearch"
//       resultCode = "403"
//       attributes.DesignMode    = "True"
//       attributes.channelId     = "pva-studio"
//       attributes.conversationId
//   Microsoft's documented Copilot Studio environment-level telemetry schema
//   publishes something different: type = "GenAI", name = "ExecuteTool", and
//   custom dimension keys prefixed "gen_ai." (gen_ai.conversation.id,
//   gen_ai.tool.name, and so on).
//   The observed shape matches NEITHER documented schema. Until this query is
//   run, no dashboard, alert, or attribution query built on either naming
//   convention can be trusted.
//   Research: .copilot-tracking/research/2026-09-22/ai-search-scaling-206-403-rca-research.md
//             Line 351 (span-shape mismatch warning), Lines 425-440 (U8)
//
// TARGET TABLE
//   Application Insights `dependencies` (the Copilot Studio telemetry export
//   target). In this engagement the component is shared across Copilot Studio,
//   Azure AI Search, and the Functions ingestion pipeline, so expect rows from
//   more than one producer.
//
// PREREQUISITES
//   * Copilot Studio telemetry export to Application Insights is enabled.
//   * "Log conversation details" is ON if you also want tool arguments and
//     results later (not required for this query).
//   * The Application Insights component does NOT have DisableLocalAuth set.
//     When it is set, Copilot Studio telemetry export fails SILENTLY and this
//     query returns zero rows even though the agent is serving traffic.
//   Enable with: scripts/Enable-DiagnosticSettings.ps1
//
// HEALTHY VS UNHEALTHY
//   Healthy   : rows returned; at least one triple clearly maps to Azure AI
//               Search; Failures is a small fraction of Calls.
//   Unhealthy : a Search-related triple where Failures / Calls is material, or
//               SampleRc shows "403", "206", "429", or "503".
//   Blocked   : zero rows. Telemetry export is off, DisableLocalAuth is set, or
//               you are querying the wrong Application Insights component. Fix
//               that before running anything else in this library.
//
// WHAT TO DO WITH THE RESULT
//   Record the winning (type, name, target) triple. Files 20-23 and 10-12 tell
//   you which literal values to substitute if yours differ from the observed
//   shape encoded here.
//
// Derived from Q6-0c-DiscoverDependencyTypes,
//   .copilot-tracking/research/2026-09-22/ai-search-scaling-206-403-rca-research.md Lines 353-361
// =============================================================================

let lookback = 7d;
dependencies
| where timestamp > ago(lookback)
| summarize
    Calls     = count(),
    Failures  = countif(success == false),
    SampleRc  = take_any(resultCode),
    ResultCodes = make_set(resultCode, 10),
    FirstSeen = min(timestamp),
    LastSeen  = max(timestamp)
    by type, name, target
| extend FailurePct = round(100.0 * Failures / Calls, 2)
| order by Calls desc

// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// COMPANION A: which custom dimension keys actually exist
// Answers "is it attributes.conversationId or gen_ai.conversation.id here?"
// Microsoft-published discovery pattern.
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// let lookback = 7d;
// dependencies
// | where timestamp > ago(lookback)
// | mv-expand Key = bag_keys(customDimensions) to typeof(string)
// | summarize
//     SeenOnSpans = make_set(name, 10),
//     SampleValue = take_any(tostring(customDimensions[Key]))
//     by Key
// | order by Key asc

// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// COMPANION B: full column list for the dependencies table
// Use when a column referenced in a downstream query errors as unknown.
// -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// dependencies
// | getschema
// | project ColumnName, ColumnType
// | order by ColumnName asc
